NAME
       mktemp - make a temporary file or directory with a unique name

SYNOPSIS
       mktemp [-d] [-u] [-q] [-p DIR] [-t] [TEMPLATE]

DESCRIPTION
       mktemp creates a new, empty file (or directory with -d) whose name
       cannot clash with an existing one, and prints its path. The TEMPLATE
       ends in at least three X characters, which are replaced by random
       letters and digits; without a template the name is tmp.XXXXXXXXXX in
       /tmp. The file is readable only by you (mode 600, directories 700).

       Scripts use it to get a safe scratch file: tmp=$(mktemp).

OPTIONS
       -d, --directory
              Make a directory instead of a file.

       -u, --dry-run
              Only print a name; create nothing (unsafe for real use).

       -q, --quiet
              Do not print errors.

       -p DIR, --tmpdir[=DIR]
              Create the name inside DIR (default $TMPDIR or /tmp).

       -t     Treat TEMPLATE as a name to put in the temporary directory.

EXAMPLES
           tmp=$(mktemp)
           work=$(mktemp -d /tmp/build.XXXXXX)

SEE ALSO
       mkdir(1), bash(1)
